{
    "file": "Customer_Satisfaction_and_Loyalty.docx",
    "title": "Customer Satisfaction and Loyalty",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Customer satisfaction and loyalty are created through the cumulative quality of the customer’s experience rather than through a single transaction. Organizations that understand customer expectations, consistently deliver relevant value, reduce unnecessary effort, respond effectively when problems occur, and learn systematically from feedback are better positioned to retain customers and build long-term relationships.",
        "This course provides participants with a practical framework for understanding, measuring, and improving customer satisfaction and loyalty. It explores customer expectations, perceived value, moments of truth, customer journeys, satisfaction drivers, service quality, trust, emotional connection, complaint handling, service recovery, customer feedback, loyalty behavior, retention, and the use of customer data to guide improvement.",
        "Participants will apply the concepts through customer-experience analysis, journey mapping, satisfaction measurement exercises, complaint and recovery scenarios, loyalty-driver analysis, and action planning. The focus is on converting customer insight into practical improvements that strengthen satisfaction, retention, advocacy, and sustainable customer relationships."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Customer-service managers and employees, customer-experience professionals, sales and account-management personnel, branch and contact-center teams, marketing professionals, service-quality personnel, operations managers, supervisors, team leaders, and employees responsible for customer satisfaction, retention, loyalty, complaint management, or service improvement."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "The course uses an interactive methodology combining short presentations, customer-experience case studies, satisfaction-driver analysis, customer-journey mapping, persona and expectation exercises, complaint and service-recovery scenarios, customer-feedback analysis, measurement activities, loyalty and retention exercises, group discussions, and action planning. Participants will apply the tools to realistic customer situations and identify practical improvements relevant to their own service environment."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Customer-centric thinking",
        "Customer expectation management",
        "Customer experience analysis",
        "Customer satisfaction measurement",
        "Service quality improvement",
        "Customer communication",
        "Complaint handling",
        "Service recovery",
        "Customer loyalty development",
        "Customer retention",
        "Customer feedback analysis",
        "Continuous service improvement"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Explain the relationship between customer expectations, perceived value, satisfaction, loyalty, and retention.",
        "Identify the principal factors that influence customer satisfaction across different touchpoints.",
        "Analyze customer journeys and recognize moments that have a disproportionate effect on satisfaction.",
        "Manage customer expectations through clear communication and reliable service delivery.",
        "Apply appropriate methods for collecting and interpreting customer feedback.",
        "Use common customer-satisfaction and loyalty measures appropriately.",
        "Handle complaints and service failures in ways that support recovery and relationship preservation.",
        "Identify the drivers of customer loyalty and the causes of customer defection.",
        "Develop practical approaches for strengthening customer retention and advocacy.",
        "Translate customer insight into prioritized service-improvement actions."
    ],
